@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Microsoft YaHei
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
title S02-ddd-sequence — source snapshot (not a runtime trace)
participant "obj: 调用者" as obj
participant "ctl: DirectoryController" as ctl
participant "svc: DirectoryApplicationService" as svc
participant "auth: AuthorizationApplicationService" as auth
participant "repo: AuthorizationRepository" as repo
participant "user: User" as user
participant "audit: AuditApplicationService" as audit
participant "directory: DirectoryRepository" as directory
participant "organization: OrganizationPolicy" as organization
participant "eligibility: DepartmentEligibility" as eligibility
participant "integrity: GrantIntegrityService" as integrity
activate obj
obj -> ctl: 1. assign(bearer, userId, input)
activate ctl
ctl -> svc: 2. assign(principal, userId, roleId)
activate svc
group local write transaction
svc -> repo: 3. lockGrants()
activate repo
deactivate repo
svc -> auth: 4. require(principal, rbac:assignment:edit, false)
activate auth
deactivate auth
svc -> directory: 5. user(userId, true)
activate directory
deactivate directory
note over svc
managed(actor, department) checks OrganizationPolicy scope.
end note
alt department is disabled
svc -> organization: 6. requireAccepting(department)
activate organization
organization --> obj: DEPARTMENT_DISABLED; abort
deactivate organization
else department accepts assignments
svc -> organization: 7. requireAccepting(department)
activate organization
deactivate organization
end
svc -> repo: 8. role(roleId)
activate repo
deactivate repo
svc -> repo: 9. systemEnabled(systemCode)
activate repo
deactivate repo
note over svc
Disabled target system throws ROLE_DISABLED.
end note
svc -> svc: 10. requireRoleWithin(actor, role)
activate svc
svc -> auth: 11. upperBound(actor, systemCode, proposed)
activate auth
deactivate auth
deactivate svc
svc -> repo: 12. eligibility(departmentId)
activate repo
deactivate repo
alt user inactive / department mismatch
svc -> user: 13. assign(role, eligibility)
activate user
user --> obj: DomainException; abort / rollback
deactivate user
else user admits assignment
svc -> user: 14. assign(role, eligibility)
activate user
user -> eligibility: 15. requireEligible(role)
activate eligibility
deactivate eligibility
deactivate user
note over eligibility
Missing eligibility or disabled role throws here.
User then rejects duplicate direct assignment; all exceptions
abort before DirectoryRepository.assign.
end note
svc -> directory: 16. assign(userId, roleId, actor.id())
activate directory
deactivate directory
end
svc -> integrity: 17. requireAdministrator()
activate integrity
deactivate integrity
svc -> repo: 18. advanceVersion()
activate repo
deactivate repo
svc -> audit: 19. local(actor, rbac-center, ROLE_ASSIGNED, subject, SUCCESS, null)
activate audit
deactivate audit
end
note over svc
Assignment, administrator-integrity check, version and SUCCESS audit
share the transaction; exceptions cannot commit a partial success.
end note
deactivate svc
deactivate ctl
deactivate obj
@enduml